{
 "turns": [
  {
   "idx": 0,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Hi, mister. Washington, come on back. Before we get going, can you confirm your full name and date of birth for me?",
   "start": 0.08,
   "end": 6.6
  },
  {
   "idx": 1,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Darnell Washington, February 9th, 1968.",
   "start": 7.2,
   "end": 10.98
  },
  {
   "idx": 2,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Perfect, thank you. How was the drive -in? I heard the parking garage was full again this morning.",
   "start": 12.2,
   "end": 17.12
  },
  {
   "idx": 3,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Oh, it was. I circled three times and ended up on the street two blocks down.",
   "start": 17.99,
   "end": 23.23
  },
  {
   "idx": 4,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Sorry about that, so this is your blood pressure follow -up. How have things been since we saw you in July?",
   "start": 24.17,
   "end": 29.19
  },
  {
   "idx": 5,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Pretty good mostly. I've been checking it at home like you said, and it's still kind of high. Usually like 145, 150 on the top number.",
   "start": 30.03,
   "end": 39.97
  },
  {
   "idx": 6,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Okay, that's helpful. And what are you taking for it right now?",
   "start": 40.49,
   "end": 43.67
  },
  {
   "idx": 7,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "The lisinopril 10 milligrams in the morning. Wait, no, it's 20. You bumped it up last time, remember? I've got the new bottle in the car.",
   "start": 44.25,
   "end": 53.19
  },
  {
   "idx": 8,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Right, twenty milligrams once a day. Are you taking it every day?",
   "start": 53.19,
   "end": 57.49
  },
  {
   "idx": 9,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Every day. I keep it next to the coffee maker, so I don't forget.",
   "start": 58.62,
   "end": 62.3
  },
  {
   "idx": 10,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Good trick, and you're still on the atorvastatin for your cholesterol.",
   "start": 63.06,
   "end": 66.06
  },
  {
   "idx": 11,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Yeah, forty milligrams at night. That one I never miss.",
   "start": 66.96,
   "end": 70.16
  },
  {
   "idx": 12,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Great. Any headaches, chest pain, or trouble catching your breath?",
   "start": 71.34,
   "end": 74.3
  },
  {
   "idx": 13,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "No, none of that.",
   "start": 75.14,
   "end": 76.3
  },
  {
   "idx": 14,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Any dizziness when you stand up or swelling in your ankles?",
   "start": 76.9,
   "end": 79.48
  },
  {
   "idx": 15,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Nope.",
   "start": 80.4,
   "end": 80.72
  },
  {
   "idx": 16,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Any cough since you've been on the listen, April. Some people get a dry, tickly cough with it.",
   "start": 81.5,
   "end": 86.6
  },
  {
   "idx": 17,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Nah, no cough.",
   "start": 87.12,
   "end": 87.96
  },
  {
   "idx": 18,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "How about salt? Last time you said you eat out a lot for lunch.",
   "start": 88.64,
   "end": 91.8
  },
  {
   "idx": 19,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Um, yeah, still work lunches. Lots of deli sandwiches and chips. I know, I know.",
   "start": 92.8,
   "end": 97.98
  },
  {
   "idx": 20,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "And alcohols.",
   "start": 98.94,
   "end": 99.9
  },
  {
   "idx": 21,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "A couple beers on the weekend, that's about it.",
   "start": 100.34,
   "end": 103.28
  },
  {
   "idx": 22,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Okay, and you mentioned your dad before, right?",
   "start": 104.08,
   "end": 106.24
  },
  {
   "idx": 23,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Yeah, my father had a stroke at 62. That's kind of why my wife Lorraine stays on me about all this.",
   "start": 106.84,
   "end": 113.72
  },
  {
   "idx": 24,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "That makes sense, she's looking out for you. All right, your blood pressure today is 152 over 94, and when I rechecked it after you sat quietly for five minutes, it was 148 over 92. Pulse is 72. Weight is 214 pounds, that's up three pounds from July.",
   "start": 114.24,
   "end": 130.92
  },
  {
   "idx": 25,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Yeah, that's the Halloween candy starting early, I guess.",
   "start": 131.76,
   "end": 135.06
  },
  {
   "idx": 26,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Let me take a listen. Heart sounds regular, no murmurs, lungs are clear and no swelling in your legs. I also have your labs from last week. Your potassium was 4 .4 and your kidney function was normal, creator 9 -0 .9. And your LDL cholesterol was 88.",
   "start": 135.06,
   "end": 152.1
  },
  {
   "idx": 27,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Is that good?",
   "start": 152.96,
   "end": 153.68
  },
  {
   "idx": 28,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "The cholesterol is right where we want it. And the kidneys and potassium look fine, which means we have room to go up on the lisson aprol. Okay. So here's what I'm thinking. Your blood pressure is still above our goal of under 130 over 80, even on the 20 milligrams. I'd like to increase the lisson -april to 40 milligrams once a day. Until you run out, you can take two of your 20s together in the morning.",
   "start": 154.36,
   "end": 179.39
  },
  {
   "idx": 29,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Two of the 20s? Got it.",
   "start": 179.85,
   "end": 181.91
  },
  {
   "idx": 30,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Keep the atorvastatin the same, 40 milligrams at night. I'd also like you to cut back on salt, aim for less than 2000 milligrams a day. The deli meat and chips are big ones.",
   "start": 182.41,
   "end": 193.03
  },
  {
   "idx": 31,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "I can try packing lunch. Lorraine will be thrilled.",
   "start": 193.59,
   "end": 196.51
  },
  {
   "idx": 32,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "That would help a lot. Since we're raising the dose, I want to repeat potassium and kidney check in about two weeks. You can go to our lab on Brookfield Avenue, no appointment needed.",
   "start": 197.48,
   "end": 207.12
  },
  {
   "idx": 33,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "I'm off on the 19th, does that work?",
   "start": 207.7,
   "end": 210.2
  },
  {
   "idx": 34,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "The 19th is perfect. Keep checking at home and bring your log next time. If you get readings over 180 on the top or a severe headache, chest pain or weakness on one side, call us or go to the emergency room.",
   "start": 210.92,
   "end": 223.64
  },
  {
   "idx": 35,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Will do.",
   "start": 224.12,
   "end": 224.66
  },
  {
   "idx": 36,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "And I'll see you back in six weeks. Is your cell still 555 -0163?",
   "start": 225.46,
   "end": 230.32
  },
  {
   "idx": 37,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Yep same number.",
   "start": 231.42,
   "end": 232.4
  },
  {
   "idx": 38,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Great any other questions for me?",
   "start": 233.06,
   "end": 234.76
  },
  {
   "idx": 39,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "No I think that's it, thanks Doc.",
   "start": 235.28,
   "end": 237.62
  },
  {
   "idx": 40,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Take care Darnell, good luck with the parking on the way out.",
   "start": 238.44,
   "end": 241.5
  }
 ],
